DuolaWork — Interim Licensing Status

Copyright (c) 2026 DuolaWork contributors.

This file is an interim licensing-status notice for this revision. It is not
a finalized source-available license and does not make a new public license
grant. Rights in original DuolaWork material are reserved, subject to any
previously valid grants and applicable third-party licenses.

The approved publication direction is a source-available foundation alongside
separately licensed commercial offerings. The intended foundation includes
the local workbench, connector and tool specifications, collaboration state
machine, handoff validation, and shared-file protocol. Planned commercial
offerings include managed hosting and enterprise capabilities.

The intended free-use policy covers personal and small-team self-use,
modification, and self-hosting. The exact eligibility criteria and the
treatment of internal commercial use have not been finalized. Commercial
resale, redistribution, and hosted-service rights are intended to require
separately agreed terms. These intentions are not a substitute for a license
grant; no team-size threshold, pricing, or production-use grant is supplied
by this notice.

This notice does not revoke or alter any license validly granted for a prior
revision, nor does it relicense third-party code, dependencies, or assets.
The repository history still contains the earlier MIT notice. Publication
of a final license and selection of public release contents remain pending.
